agm: 1.0
package: api.patterns
version: 0.2.0
title: API Pattern Examples

node api.example.pagination_cursor
type: example
summary: illustrates cursor-based pagination for a large dataset endpoint
priority: normal
stability: high
detail:
  Cursor pagination encodes the last-seen position in an opaque token.
  This avoids offset drift when items are inserted or deleted between pages.

  Request:
    GET /api/v1/events?limit=20&cursor=eyJpZCI6IjEyMzQifQ

  Response:
    {
      "data": [...],
      "next_cursor": "eyJpZCI6IjE1NTQifQ",
      "has_more": true
    }

  When has_more is false or next_cursor is absent, the client has reached
  the end of the result set.
notes:
  Cursors are base64-encoded JSON and must be treated as opaque by clients.
  Never parse or construct cursors on the client side.
